notes.text:
Decisions made when the work started. A node takes at most one name before `{`, so `cell 3 4 { ... }` would change `lang`. A cell names its place with `at R C` instead:

```acre
matrix m {
    at 40 40; rows 13; columns 12; unit 24 24;
    row-numbers 0 1; column-numbers 0 1;
    cells scores r c score;
    cell { at 3 4; fill #fde8e8; stroke #d00000; dash 4 2; }
}
```

- `matrix` takes `fill`, `stroke`, `stroke-width`, `dash`, `text-size`, `text-color` and `font` for every cell. A `cell` child overrides them for one cell, and a cell with its own outline draws above its neighbours.
- `row-numbers` and `column-numbers` take the first number and the step.
- `cells DATA RCOL CCOL TEXTCOL;` sets each cell's text from a data file (acre-4d72e1), one cell per row of the file.
- A `line`, an `arrow` or a `brace` addresses one cell as `m R C`.
- Per-cell timeline actions and an anti-diagonal selector stay open. A timeline moves, fades and colours the matrix as one.
